c07,limpio,qwen3:1.7b,zero_shot,1.0,,40,,0,122,1576,781,8.349571299972013,0.0,"15

**Step-by-Step Explanation:**

1. **Calculate total transported so far:**  
   $ 9 \text{ trips} \times 64 \text{ kg} = 576 \text{ kg} $

2. **Calculate remaining material:**  
   $ 1487 \text{ kg} - 576 \text{ kg} = 911 \text{ kg} $

3. **Determine minimum trips for remaining material:**  
   - Divide $ 911 \text{ kg} $ by $ 64 \text{ kg/trip} $:  
     $ 911 \div 64 = 14.2656 \ldots $  
   - Since partial trips are allowed, use $ 14 \text{ full trips} $ (carrying $ 14 \times 64 = 896 \text{ kg} $) and $ 1 \text{ additional trip} $ for the remaining $ 15 \text{ kg} $.

4. **Total additional trips needed:**  
   $ 14 + 1 = 15 $ trips.

**Answer:**  
$$
\boxed{15}
$$",15,15,True,,,2b
c07,limpio,qwen3:1.7b,zero_shot,1.0,,40,,1,122,2317,1413,11.502152199973352,0.0,"El número de viajes adicionales necesarios se calcula dividiendo el peso剩余 (911 kg) entre el peso máximo por viaje (64 kg), redondeando hacia arriba. 

$$
\left\lceil \frac{911}{64} \right\rceil = 15
$$

Por lo tanto, el número mínimo de viajes adicionales es **15**.

**Respuesta:**  
$$
\boxed{15}
$$",15,15,True,,,2b
c07,limpio,qwen3:1.7b,zero_shot,1.0,,40,,2,122,1458,845,7.786001899978146,0.0,"15

